  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_031 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) is the best result at 0.678 acc, showing scvi_n200 substantially outperforms pca_n2000 (0.639) and scgpt (0.525) as the RNA encoder. For the image side, resnet50 and ViT-L were nearly equivalent with pca_n2000 (0.639 vs 0.635), but that comparison was made with a weaker RNA encoder. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder to ViT-L provide additional benefit when paired with the stronger scvi_n200 RNA encoder, potentially shifting the modality balance? This is a single-variable change from the current best, keeping all other settings (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) at their validated optimal values. It is the best next experiment because it directly exploits the strongest evidence while testing the one remaining unexplored interaction (best RNA encoder × best image encoder), and the outcome—whether ViT-L helps or not—will clarify whether further image-side improvements are worthwhile under the limited budget."
}

